TP-LINK GPL code readme
 
1. This package contains all GPL code used by TP-LINK Routers with Linux OS.
2. All components have been built successfully on Ubuntu 18.04 Workstation. 
3. Compiling components in this package on platforms other than Ubuntu 18.04 Workstation may cause unexpected results. 
4. Recommended using "root" or "sudo" command to build the code. 
5. After building the code, you will get the uboot, linux kernel, rootfs and image, but you can't upgrade these images to your router through web management page. 
 
Build Command 
1. All build targets are in ./bba_3_0_platform/platform/build/, you should enter this directory to build components. 
2. Enter "make SHELL=/bin/bash MODEL=EX530v SPEC=EU1 env_build boot_build kernel_build modules_build apps_build fs_build image_build"

Required dependencies (Ubuntu Server 18.04.6:
apt install qemu-guest-agent git-lfs build-essential python2.7 zlib1g-dev uuid-dev libncurses-dev gawk flex bison openssl libssl-dev dkms libelf-dev libudev-dev libpci-dev libiberty-dev autoconf llvm device-tree-compiler tcl gettext libtool cmake autogen pkgconf rename zip texinfo
dpkg --add-architecture i386 && apt update
apt install libc6:i386 libncurses5:i386 libstdc++6:i386 zlib1g:i386 zlib1g-dev:i386 gcc-multilib g++-multilib 
